MRID_DefaultHorse: Horse
MRID_H_DefaultHorse: Used for riding and transport, this\nDagdan animal is rugged and needs\nvery little water to keep going.
MRID_DefaultOrnius: Ornius
MRID_H_DefaultOrnius: A large bird found throughout\nDagda, its strong legs allow it to\nleap and fly short distances.
MRID_DefaultPegasus: Pegasus
MRID_H_DefaultPegasus: A winged horse that is beautiful to\nbehold as it soars through the skies.\nOnly allows women to ride it.
MRID_DefaultBaw: Bau
MRID_H_DefaultBaw: A dragon with gauzy wings whose\nfierce, carnivorous temperament\nmakes it highly valued in combat.
MRID_DefaultDagdaElephant: War Elephant
MRID_H_DefaultDagdaElephant: A trained elephant that is delicate\nbut ferocious. To ride it, one needs\na special qualification.
MRID_Horse: Wild Horse
MRID_H_Horse: This horse may be a touch unruly\nto start, but an experienced rider\ncan turn it into a loyal partner.
MRID_BloodHorse: Ferghanan Horse
MRID_H_BloodHorse: A muscular, crimson-colored horse\nthat generals have sought out as a\nmount since antiquity.
MRID_BlackHorse: Black Horse
MRID_H_BlackHorse: This horse's flowing black hair\nslices through the air as it gallops\nbriskly on powerful legs.
MRID_Unicorn: Monoceros
MRID_H_Unicorn: A horse with a magnificent horn,\nthis vanishingly rare species is said\nto bring its rider good fortune.
MRID_Ornius: Wild Ornius
MRID_H_Ornius: A large, wild bird found all over the\ncontinent. Very territorial, but can\nbe coaxed into companionship.
MRID_WhiteOrnius: White Ornius
MRID_H_WhiteOrnius: This unusual variant of ornius can\nward off magic with its feathers.\nA "messenger of the gods" in myth.
MRID_Meganius: Meganius
MRID_H_Meganius: Though it looks like a regular\nornius, this variant has much more\nstrength and stamina.
MRID_RedMeganius: Red Meganius
MRID_H_RedMeganius: Though it is powerful, this ornius\nsubspecies' aggressive nature\nmakes it difficult to handle.
MRID_Maginius: Magonius
MRID_H_Maginius: A rare ornius imbued with magic.\nIt's hypothesized that this ability\ncomes from its diet.
MRID_BlackMaginius: Black Magonius
MRID_H_BlackMaginius: A rare ornius imbued with magic,\nalbeit less than the normal variant.\nIts agility makes it a popular mount.
MRID_Pegasus: Wild Pegasus
MRID_H_Pegasus: A wild winged horse with a natural\nintuition for the winds. The species\nis resistant to magic.
MRID_DarkPegasus: Dark Pegasus
MRID_H_DarkPegasus: Considered ominous by some due\nto its dark coat, this species holds\nmagical power in its body.
MRID_Falcon: Falicorn
MRID_H_Falcon: The mount of every pegasus rider's\ndreams, sought out for its superior\nstrength and swiftness.
MRID_RedFalcon: Red Falicorn
MRID_H_RedFalcon: Though its fiery features suggest\na violent attitude, this species is\ncalm and attentive to riders.
MRID_Baw: Wild Bau
MRID_H_Baw: Often used by militaries, this\nagile species became powerful\nby competing for survival.
MRID_RedBaw: Red Bau
MRID_H_RedBaw: The crimson tyrant of the skies.\nStrong and highly maneuverable,\nso it fetches a steep price.
MRID_BlackBaw: Black Bau
MRID_H_BlackBaw: Inspiring fear across the battlefield,\nthis creature blends into the\ndarkness of night to strike its foes.
MRID_DagdaElephant: Saramis War Elephant
MRID_H_DagdaElephant: Generations of careful breeding\nhave made the kingdom's elephants\nthe most powerful in Dagda.
MRID_IioHorse: Rocinan
MRID_H_IioHorse: Io's beloved steed. Old, gentle, and\nwise, he is quick to respond to\nthe will of his rider.
MRID_IioHorseAnother: Rocinan's Brother
MRID_H_IioHorseAnother: The brother of Io's beloved steed.\nOld and docile, but clever enough\nto read his rider's intentions.
MRID_AlePegasus: Bucephalus
MRID_H_AlePegasus: Alexandra's pegasus since\nchildhood, able to read his master's\nemotions and show unity in battle.
MRID_AlePegasusAnother: Bucephalus's Foal
MRID_H_AlePegasusAnother: The foal of Alexandra's pegasus,\nable to read its master's emotions\nand show unity in battle.